# Repository structure

Keep this layout. Do not flatten into a single file. Do not add RAG, DB, auth, or multi-turn unless explicitly requested.

```text
software-estimation/
├── app/
│   ├── main.py                 # FastAPI app, lifespan, /health, include routers
│   ├── config.py               # Pydantic Settings from .env
│   ├── routers/                # HTTP only (no LLM calls)
│   │   └── estimations.py      # POST /estimate
│   ├── services/               # Business / LLM logic (no HTTP)
│   │   └── llm_service.py      # LiteLLM provider-agnostic I/O
│   ├── prompts/                # Versioned Jinja2 estimation templates
│   │   ├── loader.py           # render_estimation_prompt(request, version)
│   │   └── estimation/v1|v2/   # system.j2, user.j2, examples.j2
│   └── schemas/                # Pydantic request/response models
│       ├── estimation.py       # API request/response
│       └── llm.py              # LLM JSON payload + LLMResult
├── docs/                       # Project documentation
├── .devcontainer/              # Dev Containers (Cursor / VS Code)
├── tests/
│   ├── unit/                   # Fast isolated tests
│   ├── integration/            # API boundaries (TestClient, mocked LLM)
│   ├── prompts/                # Jinja template render tests (no LLM)
│   └── e2e/                    # Critical full-stack / container flows
├── .github/workflows/ci.yml    # Docker-first CI
├── .cursor/rules/              # Cursor rules (testing, security-fastapi/python, PEP practices, …)
├── Dockerfile
├── docker-compose.yml          # api + Streamlit form
├── .dockerignore
├── .env.example                # No real secrets
├── .gitignore                  # Must include .env
├── streamlit_app.py            # Streamlit estimation form
├── Makefile
├── pyproject.toml
├── uv.lock
└── README.md
```

## Placement rules

| Change | Put it in |
|---|---|
| New HTTP endpoint | `app/routers/` + wire in `main.py` |
| LLM provider I/O | `app/services/llm_service.py` |
| Versioned Jinja2 prompts / few-shots | `app/prompts/estimation/<version>/` + `loader.py` |
| Request/response shapes | `app/schemas/` |
| Env settings | `app/config.py` + `.env.example` |
| Automated tests | `tests/unit|integration|prompts|e2e/` (see `testing-*.mdc`) |
| CI | `.github/workflows/` |
| Container | `Dockerfile` / `.dockerignore` |

## Boundaries

- Routers call services; services never import FastAPI routers or `Request`/`Response`
- Prompt templates are data under `app/prompts/`; no network I/O in the loader beyond logging
- API keys only via env / Settings — never hardcode
